// Per-stock SellShares thresholds, expressed inline with an
// `if/then/else` expression. Selling AMZN is capped at 10 shares;
// every other ticker is capped at 1000.
//
// New idea: an `if cond then a else b` expression can be used
// anywhere a value is expected inside a Cedar body. Both branches
// must produce the same type — here both are Bool.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"SellShares",
    resource
)
when {
    if context.input.stock == "AMZN"
    then context.input.shares <= 10
    else context.input.shares <= 1000
};
